# =============================================================================
# UNIVERSAL PROJECT .gitignore — conservative, multi-language baseline
#
# Covers common OS/editor noise, local environments, build outputs and caches
# across Python, JavaScript/TypeScript, C/C++, C#/.NET, Java, Go, Rust, Ruby,
# PHP, R, Julia, MATLAB, Swift, Dart/Flutter, Unity, Unreal, Godot and common
# data-science tooling.
#
# IMPORTANT
# - No .gitignore can safely cover every language/tool/project. Use the
#   companion sync-github-gitignore-templates.sh to fetch the latest official
#   GitHub templates and append the specific templates your project needs.
# - Review every rule before committing. Some projects intentionally use
#   directories named build, dist, target, logs, bin, or obj.
# - Useful source, configuration, models, datasets, notebooks, media and assets
#   are NOT ignored by this baseline merely because they are large or binary.
# - In particular, data/, datasets/, models/, checkpoints/, artifacts/,
#   Content/, Assets/, Source/, *.onnx, *.npz, *.npy, *.uasset and *.umap remain
#   trackable. Use Git LFS via .gitattributes + push-to-github.sh for large files.
# - Dependency lockfiles are intentionally retained (package-lock.json,
#   pnpm-lock.yaml, yarn.lock, poetry.lock, uv.lock, Cargo.lock, etc.).
# - Never commit passwords, tokens, private keys, production credentials or
#   private datasets you are not authorized to redistribute.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operating systems
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100/
.Trashes/
.fseventsd/
.VolumeIcon.icns
.com.apple.timemachine.donotpresent

# Windows
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
ehthumbs_vista.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# Linux / desktop environments
.directory
.Trash-*/
.nfs*

